10
01:02:36,521 --> 01:02:42,521
Carlito's Way is a 1993 American crime drama film directed by Brian De Palma and written by David Koepp,
based on the novels Carlito's Way (1975) and After Hours (1979) by Judge Edwin Torres.

11
01:08:52,173 --> 01:08:58,173
It stars Al Pacino, Sean Penn, Penelope Ann Miller, Luis Guzman, John
Leguizamo, Jorge Porcel, Joseph Siravo and Viggo Mortensen.

12
01:15:07,826 --> 01:15:13,826
Pacino portrays Carlito Brigante, a Nuyorican criminal who
vows to go straight and to retire in Paradise.

13
01:21:23,478 --> 01:21:29,478
However, his criminal past proves difficult to escape, and he is unwillingly dragged
into the same activities that got him imprisoned in the first place.

14
01:27:39,130 --> 01:27:45,130
The film is based mainly on After Hours, but it used the title of the first
novel to avoid it being confused with Martin Scorsese's 1985 film.

15
01:33:54,782 --> 01:34:00,782
This is the second film collaboration with Pacino
and De Palma, after Scarface (1983).

16
01:40:10,434 --> 01:40:16,434
Carlito's Way was released on November 12, 1993, by Universal Pictures.

17
01:46:26,086 --> 01:46:32,086
It initially received mixed reviews from critics and lukewarm results at the box office,
although general reception to the film has improved in subsequent years.

18
01:52:41,739 --> 01:52:47,739
The film has gained a strong cult following, and it is generally
considered to be one of De Palma's most enduring films.

19
01:58:57,391 --> 01:59:03,391
Both Penn and Miller received Golden Globe nominations for their performances.

20
02:05:13,043 --> 02:05:19,043
A prequel titled Carlito's Way: Rise to Power, based on the
first novel, was released direct-to-video in 2005.

21
02:11:28,695 --> 02:11:34,695
The film explores themes of new york city, based on novel or
book, gangster, go-go dancer, release from prison.

22
02:17:44,347 --> 02:17:50,347
The tone is intense and dark and emotional.
